* Mantis shrimp: punch so fast the water itself flashes and bubbles.
* Pistol shrimp: snap one claw and stun prey with a collapsing bubble.
* Electric eel: make electricity and use it to sense and shock.
* Skunk: manufacture a smell so awful most attackers give up.
* Porcupine: turn “don’t eat me” into thousands of sharp points.
* Bombardier ant: spray boiling acid at anything bothering it.
* Cone snail: harpoon prey with a venomous tooth.
* Hagfish: turn water into a huge cloud of slime when attacked.
* Flying fish: escape one predator by briefly becoming an air glider.
* Remora: stick to a bigger animal and get a free ride.
* Leafcutter ant: cut leaves, carry them home, and farm fungus.
* Lyrebird: copy almost any sound it hears to impress a mate.
* Wombat: make cube-shaped poop so it stays put as a territorial marker.
* Mimic octopus: pretend to be whichever dangerous animal fits the moment.
* Frogfish: grow a fishing lure on your face and wait for dinner.